     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't address either problem. You aren't the prescriber, and 5,100 mg per day is about double the maximum daily dose. That is a real risk of serious harm to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a corrected order** if the prescriber gives me one. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg per day and is within the usual maximum.\n- **Help you reach the right person.** The prescriber or the medicine service pharmacist can confirm the intended dose. If the order came from a clinician, they can resubmit it directly or tell me the corrected dose.\n\nIf the prescriber has reviewed this and really intends 1,700 mg three times daily, they should enter it themselves. That way the order goes through the hospital's clinical safety checks and carries their accountability. I'm not willing to enter it for a non-clinician."
      }
     ],
